  "version": 1,
  "description": "Committed device enrollment (spec §3.9). join = \"akj2-\" || b64(cjson({\"v\":1,\"ctx\":\"akv1/enroll-join\",\"account\",\"device\",\"nonce_j_commit\",\"label\"})); offer = \"ako2-\" || b64(cjson({\"v\":1,\"ctx\":\"akv1/enroll-offer\",\"vault_origin\",\"vault_id\",\"initiator\",\"joiner\",\"nonce_i\",\"nonce_j_commit\",\"trust_anchor\",\"checkpoint\"})); reveal = \"akr2-\" || b64(cjson({\"v\":1,\"ctx\":\"akv1/enroll-reveal\",\"vault_id\",\"joiner\",\"nonce_j\"})). join, offer and reveal: encoding the object MUST give the code byte for byte and parsing the code MUST give the object back. Parsing follows the §3.8 order (every failure bad_request except the code own v: unsupported_version) with the keys and contexts above; nonce_j_commit is 32 bytes; a reveal names vault_id and the joiner device_id and carries a 16-byte nonce_j. commit: nonce_j_commit = b64(sha256(cjson({\"ctx\":\"akv1/enroll-nonce-j\",\"nonce_j\"}))). reveal_check: verifying nonce_j against commit MUST pass when expect is ok and fail with the given code otherwise. sas2: transcript_text = cjson({\"ctx\":\"akv1/sas2\",\"vault_id\",\"vault_origin\",\"trust_anchor\",\"initiator\",\"joiner\":device record,\"nonce_i\",\"nonce_j\"}); code = uint32be(sha256(transcript)[0:4]) mod 10^6 as six digits; digest = b64(sha256(transcript)) is device_add.body.sas; every field changes the digits. ground_sas: ground_nonce_j makes the sas2 code of the case equal target_code (a six-digit match found by search) but is not the nonce_j that forged_commit commits to, so verifying it against forged_commit MUST fail with forbidden; the legacy §3.5 transcript offers no such check. invalid_join, invalid_offer and invalid_reveal: parsing code_text MUST fail with expect_error.",
